\f0\b\fs58\fsmilli29333 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 CWO Admin Tool \'97 How to Use\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec3 Owner-only admin interface for live Cthulhu Wars Online games on cwo.freeddns.org.
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa365\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 \strokec2 Quick start\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec3 1. Open
\f3 admin.html
\f2  in your browser (double-click or bookmark it).\
2. Server URL is pre-filled to
\f3 https://cwo.freeddns.org
\f2 . Leave it.\
3. Paste your owner admin token (kept in
\f3 Library at Celaeno/Server Deployment/owner-admin-token.txt
\f2 ).\
4. Click
\f0\b Sign in
\f2\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa365\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 \strokec2 Game list\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec3 The main screen shows all live games sorted by
\f0\b last activity
\f2\b0  (most recently active at top). Each game card shows its name, build (Library/MNU/TT/BB/HB), player count, and last-active time.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Sorting\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Use the
\f0\b Sort
\f2\b0  dropdown at the top of the list to switch between: Last activity (default), Name A-Z, Name Z-A, Newest first, Oldest first.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Filters\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Click the filter icon to open the
\f0\b filter pyramid
\f2\b0 . Filters stack (AND logic). Available filters:\
\'95
\f0\b Build
\f2\b0  \'97 Library, MNU, TT, BB, HB (checkboxes; select multiple)\
\'95
\f0\b Status
\f2\b0  \'97 Healthy, Broken, Completed\
\'95
\f0\b Players
\f2\b0  \'97 by count\
\'95
\f0\b Bot
\f2\b0  \'97 Has bots, No bots\
Each filter option shows how many games match. Clear all with the X button.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Search\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 The search box matches against game name. Type part of a name and the list filters instantly.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Freeze\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Each game card has a
\f0\b Freeze
\f2\b0  button. Frozen games are pinned to the top of the list regardless of sort order. This persists across sessions (stored in localStorage). Use it for games you're actively monitoring.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa365\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 \strokec2 Game detail view\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec3 Click a game to open its detail view. On desktop (wide screens) the game detail takes the full width. Click the back arrow to return to the list.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Players\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Each faction is listed with a clickable link. Clicking opens that player's game view (using their secret URL) so you can see their perspective or play on their behalf.\
The
\f0\b Open as Owner
\f2\b0  button opens the game with the master secret \'97 you see every faction's state.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Faction state table\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 A scrollable table shows live state for every faction: power, doom, gates, units, spellbooks, etc. This is reconstructed from the game engine.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Console grab\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 The
\f0\b Grab Console
\f2\b0  button launches a headless Chrome session on the server to capture the game's live console output (println traces, errors). Results appear inline. Useful for debugging crashes or verifying trace output.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa365\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 \strokec2 Game log\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec3 Below the players, every log entry appears in reverse order (most recent at top). Each line shows its index, the role that wrote it, and the action.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Log view modes\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Toggle between two views:\
\'95
\f0\b Game Log
\f2\b0  \'97 shows humanized text (what the player sees) above the raw action string\
\'95
\f0\b Debug
\f2\b0  \'97 shows only the raw action string (for copy/paste or debugging)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Permanent lines (red)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Lines in red contain dice rolls, Elder Signs, or other permanent events that are normally blocked from undo. As the owner, you can roll back past them.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Roll back\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Every log line has a
\f0\b Roll back to here
\f2\b0  button. Deletes that line and everything after. Confirmation dialog appears first. Rolled-back entries are automatically stashed (see below).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Edit (generic)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Every log line has an
\f0\b Edit
\f2\b0  button. Opens the raw action string in a text input for direct editing. Save writes the modified value back to the server. Use carefully \'97 malformed actions will crash the game.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Edit ES (Elder Signs)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Lines containing Elder Sign values show an
\f0\b Edit ES
\f2\b0  button. Click it and a small input appears with just the ES value (the number). Change the number and save. The rest of the action string is preserved automatically.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Edit Battle Results\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Lines containing BattleRollAction show an
\f0\b Edit Battle
\f2\b0  button. Click it and colored chips appear below the line \'97 one per die result:\
\'95 Grey = Miss\
\'95 Amber = Pain\
\'95 Red = Kill\
Click any chip to cycle it through Miss > Pain > Kill > Miss. When you're happy with the results, click
\f0\b Save
\f2\b0 . The action is reconstructed in the correct format and saved.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa365\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 \strokec2 Stash\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec3 When you roll back, the deleted entries are automatically saved to the stash. The stash appears as a collapsible section below the game log.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Viewing stashed entries\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Stashed entries are grouped by rollback session. Each entry shows its raw action value. Click to expand/collapse groups.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Re-insert\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Each stashed entry has a
\f0\b Re-insert
\f2\b0  button. This appends that exact action back to the live game log (as a new entry at the end). Use this to replay actions after a rollback without manually redoing them in-game.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Edit stashed entries\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Each stashed entry has an
\f0\b Edit
\f2\b0  button. Modify the raw action string before re-inserting it. Useful for fixing a corrupted action before putting it back.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Delete stash group\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Delete an entire rollback group from the stash when you no longer need it. The stash persists in localStorage per game.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa365\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 \strokec2 Build switcher\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec3 The
\f0\b Build
\f2\b0  page lets you select which build is active for the SimRunner. It does
\f0\b NOT
\f2\b0  affect the game list \'97 the game list has its own Build filter checkboxes. The build switcher only controls: which build the SimRunner uses, and the little build label in the header.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa365\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 \strokec2 SimRunner\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec3 The SimRunner page lets you launch automated game simulations against the selected build.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Running a sim\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Select a preset (Library factions or MNU factions), customize the faction list if needed, set the number of iterations, and click
\f0\b Run Sim
\f2\b0 . The simulation runs on the server and results appear below.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Sim history\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Previous sim runs are listed with their parameters and results. You can review past runs without re-running them.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa365\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 \strokec2 Security notes\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec3 \'95 The owner token is the ONLY thing protecting these admin endpoints. Treat it like an email password.\
\'95 If the token leaks, anyone who has it can wipe every game on the server. Rotate it immediately.\
\'95 The token is stored at
\f3 Library at Celaeno/Server Deployment/owner-admin-token.txt
\f2  on this machine.\
\'95 The admin endpoints return HTTP 404 to anyone without the token \'97 so probing returns the same response as a non-existent URL.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa365\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 \strokec2 Token rotation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec3 If you ever want to change the token:\
1. Generate a new one: in Terminal, run
\f3 openssl rand -hex 24
\f2  and copy the output.\
2. Update
\f3 /etc/systemd/system/cwo.service
\f2  on the VM \'97 the systemd ExecStart line has the token as the last argv.\
3. Save the new token to the local
\f3 owner-admin-token.txt
\f2  file.\
4. SSH to the VM:
\f3 sudo systemctl daemon-reload && sudo systemctl restart cwo
\f2 .\
5. Sign in to
\f3 admin.html
\f2  with the new token.\
}
